layer":"furniture","label":"page_header","orig":"Computerized adaptive testing in the Bundeswehr","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":767.719970703125,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":202.33333333333334,"r":405.0,"t":782.3866373697916},"charspan":[0,47],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"Computerized adaptive testing in the Bundeswehr"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Values concerning item bank building (item linking, ~calibration; equating)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":712.3866373697916,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":89.66666666666667,"r":517.6666666666666,"t":733.3866373697916},"charspan":[0,75],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"Values concerning item bank building (item linking, ~calibration; equating)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"In a further the adaptive 2 PL-algorithm was evaluated in combination with the three item banks mentioned above. Hence 8000 examinees (draftees) worked on the usual conventional test battery . received one of the three tests which corresponded to one test in the test battery. additional test was administered as an adaptive one. step Aaditionallyỉhe they","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":477.3866373697917,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":49.666666666666664,"r":550.0,"t":552.3866373697916},"charspan":[0,355],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"In a further the adaptive 2 PL-algorithm was evaluated in combination with the three item banks mentioned above. Hence 8000 examinees (draftees) worked on the usual conventional test battery . received one of the three tests which corresponded to one test in the test battery. additional test was administered as an adaptive one. step Aaditionallyỉhe they"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The aim of adaptive testing in the testing situation is to maximum information with minimum effort. Hence the examinees should be given only those items that meet the person's level of functioning; s0 that the items will be solved in about fifty percent of the cases. If that holds; irrelevant items can be economized on, and, as one of various merits; it can be expected that adaptive testing; particularly the 2 PL; will need much less items as conventional tests based on classical test theory: The conventional tests of our test battery consist of 20 items each with moderate reliability = 0.74 to Itt 0.88) Figure 1 is based on the compound result of the three tests. It shows the joint distribution of the adaptive items needed to reach a reliability of rt > 0.84 for each person. This reliability is associated with a standard error of measurement of SEM 0.39 for this sample. With the appearance of variance in the answer vector, the SEM is calculated whenever a person answers an administered item within the adaptive testing procedure: Before testing, the SEM value is fixed on a corresponding desired reliability level (in this case Itt = 0.84). This cut-off value serves as criterion of the adaptive procedure as soon as the SEM falls below. gain against (Itt stop","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":243.719970703125,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":49.666666666666664,"r":556.3333333333334,"t":468.719970703125},"charspan":[0,1276],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The aim of adaptive testing in the testing situation is to maximum information with minimum effort. Hence the examinees should be given only those items that meet the person's level of functioning; s0 that the items will be solved in about fifty percent of the cases. If that holds; irrelevant items can be economized on, and, as one of various merits; it can be expected that adaptive testing; particularly the 2 PL; will need much less items as conventional tests based on classical test theory: The conventional tests of our test battery consist of 20 items each with moderate reliability = 0.74 to Itt 0.88) Figure 1 is based on the compound result of the three tests. It shows the joint distribution of the adaptive items needed to reach a reliability of rt > 0.84 for each person. This reliability is associated with a standard error of measurement of SEM 0.39 for this sample. With the appearance of variance in the answer vector, the SEM is calculated whenever a person answers an administered item within the adaptive testing procedure: Before testing, the SEM value is fixed on a corresponding desired reliability level (in this case Itt = 0.84). This cut-off value serves as criterion of the adaptive procedure as soon as the SEM falls below. gain against (Itt stop"}],"version":"1.10.0"}